{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"In-scope decision: the plan expected Gerrit 3428 (requires_posix_shell) to cover the 13 test_autodeploy_prune.py entries. 3428 has now merged (7e0eaf4cd1f), but it decorates only `test_the_buildkit_cap_is_not_re_spelled_in_autodeploy`. The 13 deselected tests all go through `_run_helpers`, which runs `bash -c <harness>`, and they carry no skip. So `_run_helpers` now calls `pytest.skip` when `posix_shell_available()` is false. This uses the same capability probe as the rest of the POSIX-shell class and adds no new mechanism. With that, max-path.args is empty: the change deletes it and its `@` line in test.yml. The extra file is tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py (7 lines). After the rebase onto 535e09284d3, test_autodeploy_prune, test_windows_sweep_deselect, test_snapshot_build_dir_length and test_ci_workflow_parity pass (66 tests)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795075617759239900,"uuid":"ace30135-89d4-4bc3-a98b-bd4cd42e2c2d"}